<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπαθ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			<i>have an aversion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>Pr.Prooem.</u>
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be opposed, reversed</i> in metric, as lambus or trochee, Sch.Heph.<i><span class="en">
				p.115C.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be affected,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τῶν ἔξωθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					291.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be affected in a contrary manner,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					34.9.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				3.5.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
